1. Check Git Version
git --version

2. Clone the Existing GitHub Repository
git clone https://github.com/sivapriyakumar246-cyber/GitExperiment1.git

3. Open the Repository Folder
cd GitExperiment1

4. Display the Files
dir

5. Check Repository Status
git status

6. Check the Current Branch
git branch

7. Check the Remote Repository
git remote -v

8. Create a File for Experiment 2
echo Experiment 2 - GitHub Sync > Experiment2.txt

9. Display the File Content
type Experiment2.txt

10. Add the File to the Staging Area
git add Experiment2.txt

11. Check Repository Status
git status

12. Commit the Changes
git commit -m "Experiment 2 commit"

13. Push Local Commits to GitHub
git push

14. Pull Updates from GitHub
git pull

15. Display Commit History
git log --oneline

16. Check Final Repository Status
git status
